mones in order to stimulate a woman's  reproductive cycle to get the IVF going  and in some countries there are fake  medicines you know people in Nigeria for  example are very concerned that it's not  really you know going to be efficacious  if they do it in their home country and  they're concerned about safety not just  in Nigeria but in many parts of the  world where they feel that the quality  of medical care is simply not good in  their home home country it's a safety  and efficacy and sort of quality and  doing it in a place where you feel  comfortable that is safe and you know  effective is very important and then  there are a whole host of one what we  might call sort of socio-cultural issues  people concerned about medical privacy  people actually concerned if they do IVF  in their home country that people are  going to talk about them that it won't  be confidential they don't want to be  seen by people that they might run into  an IVF clinic and so they will move and  sometimes people move just to have sort  of linguistic and cultural connection  with providers and so there are sort of  cultural subtle nuances of you know  cultural considerations and so these are  sort of four categories  why people are are traveling and  together it's a lot of reasons actually  why people would seek IVF outside of  their home country right so it seems  like it will just keep growing and  growing for Dubai yeah and around the  world they're showing that people are  traveling to parts of Latin America  people are really traveling traveling  there are now really thousands perhaps  millions of repro travelers there really  isn't a good study but the few studies  that have been done have shown that  thousands of people are traveling trying  to access IVF in other parts of the  world Wow very interesting thank you for  being here with us today for speaking  with me about my book okay and good luck  with it thank you so much Carolyn for  more information about professor in horn  and her research please visit our  website at macmillan report yale edu be  sure to join us again for another  episode of the macmillan report made  possible through funding from the  Whitney and Betty Macmillan Center for  International and area studies at Yale

